Dulcamara: a movie or sound the system gives no thread for is ready, with nothing in it.

media_start makes a decode thread for each movie and sound, and only that thread marks it ready; drawing a movie's
picture (media_read_video) waits until it is. On the PS5 the console refuses threads past a limit (0.2.8's log had
FFmpeg's refused at about 31), and a tester's game stopped answering as she moved the cursor fast over its title
menu, each button playing a sound. With no thread, the media is now ready at once with nothing in it, as one whose
file does not open is. Applied to Ren'Py 8's src/ffmedia.c and Ren'Py 7's module/ffmedia.c, the same there.

--- a/ffmedia.c
+++ b/ffmedia.c
@@ -1534,6 +1534,15 @@
 	snprintf(buf, 1024, "decode: %s", ms->filename);
 	SDL_Thread *t = SDL_CreateThread(decode_thread, buf, (void *) ms);
 	ms->thread = t;
+
+	/* Dulcamara: with no thread for it (the system refused one), it is ready with nothing in it, as a file that does
+	 * not open is; else drawing its picture (media_read_video) would wait for the thread forever. */
+	if (t == NULL) {
+		SDL_LockMutex(ms->lock);
+		ms->ready = 1;
+		SDL_CondBroadcast(ms->cond);
+		SDL_UnlockMutex(ms->lock);
+	}
 #endif
 }
 
